meta {
  name: 02 Register Subscription
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/subscription/register
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  **Register Subscription** — registers the business as a client on the subscription
  server (proxied `POST /clients`). This is the prerequisite that unlocks plans and
  bills; the equivalent of the legacy "Register Subscription" button.

  No body: the payload is built server-side from the tenant record —
  `name`, `code` (shortName), `address` (addressLine), `address_2` (area), `city`,
  `country`, `postcode` (pincode), `contact_email`, `contact_phone`, and the
  resolved `business_id`. PAN / GST / contact-person are not held on the Tenant, so
  they are sent blank (as the legacy flow did when absent).

  Returns the created client record (`data.original`). Throws
  `SUBSCRIPTION_REGISTRATION_FAILED` (502) if the server rejects the call,
  `SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_CONFIGURED` (503) when unconfigured, or
  `SUBSCRIPTION_BUSINESS_ID_MISSING` (409) when the tenant has no business id.
}
